"description":"Talkspace is an online therapy app that connects adults and teens (13+) with licensed therapists in their state for text, audio, and video therapy — covered by many U.S. insurance plans and employers.\n\nMore than 1 million people have used Talkspace for online therapy. Read member reviews at www.talkspace.com/reviews.\n\nTalkspace uses clinician-informed, responsible AI tools to support care that always stays human-first: every member is treated by a licensed therapist.\n\nHOW DOES TALKSPACE WORK?\nTell us your preferences and get matched with a licensed therapist in your state, often the same day. Send unlimited text, audio, picture, or video messages anytime and receive responses at least once a day, 5 days a week — so you can process things as they happen instead of waiting for a weekly appointment.\n\nWHAT CAN TALKSPACE HELP WITH?\nTalkspace therapists treat a wide range of mental health needs, including anxiety, depression, stress and burnout, relationship challenges, trauma and PTSD, substance use, and grief. Whatever brings you to therapy, you'll be matched with a therapist experienced in your area of need.\n\nIS TALKSPACE FOR TEENS?\nYes. Talkspace offers online therapy for teens ages 13–17 with therapists specialized in adolescent mental health — including school stress, anxiety, and self-esteem. Parental or guardian consent is required to get started.\n\nDOES TALKSPACE OFFER PSYCHIATRY OR COUPLES THERAPY?\nYes. In addition to individual therapy, Talkspace offers psychiatry (evaluation and medication management with licensed prescribers) and couples therapy — all online, in the same app.\n\nIS TALKSPACE COVERED BY INSURANCE?\nYes. Talkspace is in-network with leading U.S. health plans and partners with many employers, so most covered members pay a copay similar to an in-person visit. Enter your insurance or employer details at checkout to check eligibility in seconds.\n\nHOW MUCH DOES TALKSPACE COST?\nMany members pay only a copay through insurance. Without insurance, choose a subscription plan that fits your needs and budget. Visit our Help Center for pricing details.\n\nIS TALKSPACE EFFECTIVE?\nTalkspace has been shown to be as effective as face-to-face therapy: in one study, 81% of participants found Talkspace as effective or better than in-person therapy, and users showed significant improvement in depression and anxiety symptoms within 2 months. Talkspace has been featured in The Wall Street Journal, CNN, and Business Insider.\nResearch: research.talkspace.com | Press: talkspace.com/press\n\nWHO ARE THE TALKSPACE THERAPISTS?\nThe Talkspace network includes thousands of licensed therapists across all 50 states, all vetted and credentialed according to NCQA standards. If your first match isn't the right fit, you can switch therapists anytime.\n\nIS TALKSPACE SECURE?\nYour safety and security are our #1 priorities. Talkspace is protected with banking-grade encryption and externally audited for HIPAA compliance. Full Privacy Policy: talkspace.com/public/privacy-policy\n\nWHAT IS TALKCAST?\nTo help you stay engaged between sessions, your therapist can create Talkcast personalized podcasts: after your therapist reviews a script based on your therapy goals, our AI engine generates a custom recording you can listen to anytime.\n\nWHO IS TALKSPACE BEST FOR?\nTalkspace is ideal for anyone who wants therapy that fits a busy schedule, prefers messaging a therapist over weekly appointments, wants to use insurance for mental health care, or is starting therapy for the first time and wants a low-pressure way to begin.\n\nCONNECT WITH US\nQuestions or feedback? Email support@talkspace.com or visit talkspace.com. \nFollow Talkspace on X, Instagram, and Facebook.", "trackId":661829386, "trackName":"Talkspace: Virtual Therapy App", "userRatingCount":47310}, 
